{
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002B.title": "Scrap Barrel",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002B.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Scrap Metal in a ring. Every vanilla container needs wood, so this is the first storage this world has.",
    "",
    "It opens the ordinary chest screen and holds a chest's worth of anything.",
    "",
    "It is also the first block that can catch what the others put out. Scrap blocks touching face to face are one Scrap Network. No pipes, no wires, nothing to connect. Set the barrel against the Sorting Tarp and sifted materials land in it rather than on the floor; the same goes for whatever the Burn Barrel and the Recompile Workbench turn out.",
    "",
    "Touching means sharing a face. A block on the diagonal is a separate network, and so is one with a gap.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002C.title": "The Burn Barrel",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002C.quest_desc": [
    "Seven Scrap Metal. It is the first smelter in the world and opens the ordinary furnace screen.",
    "",
    "It takes refuse and food and nothing else, so Scrap Metal and anything edible will burn where other metals will not. Pipes and hoppers cannot reach it either, so you load it by hand.",
    "",
    "Stand a Scrap Barrel against it and the two are one Scrap Network. Finished smelts move across into the barrel as they come, so you are not standing over it to collect.",
    "",
    "It needs fuel. There is no coal and no wood in this world.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002F.title": "Fuel",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002F.quest_desc": [
    "Fiber Scrap and Organic Muck, in any arrangement. Both come out of the same garbage you are already sorting, so fuel is never the thing that stops you.",
    "",
    "One rag burns as long as charcoal does - eight items smelted. Junk burns too, at two items a piece, which is worth knowing when you are standing in a pile of it and short of rags.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002D.title": "Copper",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002D.quest_desc": [
    "Burn Scrap Metal in the barrel and it comes back as copper nuggets. Nine of those make an ingot, which is a great deal of scrap for a little metal.",
    "",
    "Copper is what this world runs on. Iron exists, but it is out past the demolition yard behind a furnace you cannot build yet.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002E.title": "A Bucket of Water",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002E.quest_desc": [
    "There is no recipe for a bucket. Vanilla's is switched off here, so you find them instead - roughly one pull in fourteen hundred out of household garbage.",
    "",
    "So this is the long one, and nothing hurries it. Keep a Sorting Tarp running and a bucket turns up in the sorting you were already doing.",
    "",
    "Fill it at the Rain Collector and you have water you can carry.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002A.title": "Dirty Mattress",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00002A.quest_desc": [
    "The commonest thing in Bulky Waste, and the only bed until you can make a clean one.",
    "",
    "Sleeping on it breaks it when you get up. Sneak-right-click instead to set your spawn point, which does not wear it out, so one mattress can be your respawn and still be there tomorrow.",
    "",
    "Tearing one down at the Workbench with a Scrap Knife gives an idea toward the Clean Mattress. Four of those and you can make the real thing.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000029.title": "The Pump",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000029.quest_desc": [
    "Find a Washing Machine in Bulky Waste and tear it down at the Workbench with a Prybar racked. It gives one Pump, plus scrap and plastic.",
    "",
    "The teardown also gives an idea toward the Pump itself. Four of those make a blueprint, and with it you can craft one from three copper, a Scrap Metal and a Plastic Scrap - so the first washing machine is the only one you have to find.",
    "",
    "It is a component of the Grass Spreader, the machine that turns coarse dirt back to grass.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000020.title": "The Scrap Crafting Table",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000020.quest_desc": [
    "There is no wood in this world, so there is no vanilla crafting table.",
    "",
    "This one is two Scrap Metal over two Fiber Scrap, which fits the 2x2 grid in your inventory. Anything with a 3x3 recipe needs it.",
    "",
    "Put it down somewhere you have room to build around. Scrap blocks set against each other work as one Scrap Network, and this table is where you look at it - the panel down the right of its screen lists what the whole network is holding. Yours is empty so far.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000021.title": "Prybar",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000021.quest_desc": [
    "Two Scrap Metal and a Rebar, small enough for your inventory grid. It opens Bulky Waste, and nothing else does.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000022.title": "Scrap Knife",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000022.quest_desc": [
    "One Scrap Metal over one Rebar, small enough for your inventory grid.",
    "",
    "It opens sealed Tin Cans, and it is the only thing that will pick up or sort a Compacted Bale.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000023.title": "Open Bulky Waste",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000023.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click it with a Prybar. It opens in one action, drops a single find, and breaks. Mining it by hand gives nothing at all.",
    "",
    "Most finds are ordinary. About one in ten comes from a better pool, and those are worth going out of your way for.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000024.title": "Something to Eat",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000024.quest_desc": [
    "Nothing spawns in the garbage biome, so there is nothing to hunt.",
    "",
    "A sealed can is not food yet. Hold the can and right-click with a Scrap Knife anywhere in your inventory - you do not have to hold the knife, and it is not used up.",
    "",
    "Dump Mushrooms grow on the mycelium between mounds, and they place back down, so a patch you replant keeps feeding you.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000025.title": "The Sorting Tarp",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000025.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click the tarp with a Block of Garbage, a Trash Bag, or a Compacted Bale in hand and it sifts that one straight out. Hold right-click to keep feeding it.",
    "",
    "A Trash Bag breaks by hand and needs no tool, so you can feed the tarp from the moment you have one. A whole Block of Garbage has to be carried here, and that needs a shovel. A Compacted Bale needs a Scrap Knife to pick up at all.",
    "",
    "Nothing crumbles in your hands this way, which is the point of it. It has no screen and stores nothing, so everything lands on the ground around it - stand somewhere you do not mind covering.",
    "",
    "A Scrap Barrel touching the tarp catches all of it instead. That is the difference between sorting and standing in a pile of your own scrap.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000026.title": "The Recompile Workbench",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000026.quest_desc": [
    "Rack both tools on it by right-clicking the bench with each in turn. It has a slot for a Scrap Knife and a slot for a Prybar, and different finds want different tools.",
    "",
    "Then hold right-click with whatever you want taken apart.",
    "",
    "The racked tool wears down as it works. When it breaks, nothing comes apart until you rack another.",
    "",
    "What comes off lands on top of the bench. Stand the bench against a Scrap Barrel and it goes into the barrel instead.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000027.title": "Junk Shovel",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000027.quest_desc": [
    "This is how you carry garbage to the tarp rather than sorting it where it stands. A Block of Garbage or a pile of Stone Rubble breaks to nothing without a shovel in hand; any shovel will do.",
    "",
    "It digs the coarse dirt faster too.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000028.title": "The Rain Collector",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000028.quest_desc": [
    "A Water Tank and a copper pipe. The tank is plastic scrap, rebar and scrap metal, so the copper is the only part you had to smelt for.",
    "",
    "Leave it under open sky and it fills when it rains. Break it and the water it holds comes with it, so moving it costs nothing.",
  ],
}
